{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1433492-the-icelus-foundation-and-psychognosis","id":1433492,"title":"The Icelus Foundation and Psychognosis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-26T05:51:48-08:00","id":1433492,"title":"The Icelus Foundation and Psychognosis","content":"So I was reading the Icelus bloodline and their whole scheme. I'm having trouble understanding the appeal, mechanically speaking.<br /> They have a merit that allow them to tap into the dreams of a subject to give them a boost in their discipline uses.<br /> <br /> The problem's I have with this are:<br /> - The victim must be willing<br /> - The willpower cost is huge<br /> - The benefits seems minor<br /> <br /> Point 1:<br /> Psychognosis only work on willing victims, wich per se is fine, but them, to have some easy access you need to use it on something that you already have like your Herd. Making it also needs a second merit for good use.<br /> <br /> Point 2:<br /> You need to spend 1WP to activate the hypnosis and 1 more for each technique, so, at least 2 WP to use the merit for a boost in a discipline. If you want to use all the benefits, this increases to 6 willpower points. You also needs to spend more willpower in certain levels to get some benefit, or vitae.<br /> <br /> Point 3:<br /> The benefits this merit gives to the disciplines are not as rewarding, some more questions on Auspex, or minus 1 to 3 dices to resist Dominate.<br /> <br /> Kindred normally don't dream. Having access to the dreams of the kine should give some way to get Willpower or other form of resource, that's the whole propaganda of the bloodline, they have discovered a way to tap into the infinite source of energy that is the dreams and use it for their own benefit. What do you guys think about the bloodline?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T07:00:44-08:00","id":1433497,"title":"","content":"The Willpower cost is up to six Willpower to give its bonuses to all the relevant uses for a night in a splat whose aura effect is optimized to give them exceptional successes and the Inspired Condition. Vampires get Willpower from being vampires. It would be one thing if the benefits only applied to the character you used the hypnotic state on, but &quot;Spend Willpower for the effects you want to use and you get them against everything for the session&quot; is not nothing.<br /> <br /> It's a Merit whose prerequisites include something characters get for free from membership in the bloodline's Mystery Cult. Breaking the limits of multiple once-per-night or once-per-scene effects is not nothing for that price, nor is ignoring multiple dots' worth of Resistance Traits, getting more answers to your basic Auspex questions for the night, and/or extending the memory-scanning power of a mind-reading Discipline to a real-time feed beyond your immediate presence are pretty swell bonuses to get for a maximum cost of five Experiences.<br /> <br /> As for willing victims, remember that this is a bloodline of <i>vampire psychotherapists</i> made up of <i>Mekhet and Ventrue</i> who run a <i>cult</i>. Functionally needing to be with a client to do the prep for using the Merit is not a huge restriction, given that \u2014 again \u2014 having any level of initiation in the Mystery Cult (much less Influence) gives you the relevant specialty and social sway with people if Vampire's wealth of &quot;get free Merits equal to your Covenant Status&quot; Merits wasn't doing its job.<br /> <br /> The bloodline has access to two clan-specific Disciplines and a particular concept. Its special trick built through the least expensive variety of Trait to purchase is allowed to be a little niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T08:01:36-08:00","id":1433504,"title":"","content":"Just to be sure. If I use the 2dot technique Diagnostic Dreaming, and use Auspex 1(Beast\u2019s Hackles), your normal success count as an exceptional success, so, you get the Inspired condition? You get Inspired from exceptional sucess on Discipline uses?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T08:08:12-08:00","id":1433507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1433492-the-icelus-foundation-and-psychognosis?p=1433504#post1433504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be sure. If I use the 2dot technique Diagnostic Dreaming, and use Auspex 1(Beast\u2019s Hackles), your normal success count as an exceptional success, so, you get the Inspired condition? You get Inspired from exceptional sucess on Discipline uses?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am saying that the Predatory Aura applies Conditions that make exceptional success easier on certain types of rolls, is free to use on mortals, and can benefit from one of three different one-dot Merits that specialize its use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T09:24:09-08:00","id":1433510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1433492-the-icelus-foundation-and-psychognosis#post1433492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was reading the Icelus bloodline and their whole scheme. I'm having trouble understanding the appeal, mechanically speaking.<br /> They have a merit that allow them to tap into the dreams of a subject to give them a boost in their discipline uses.<br /> <br /> The problem's I have with this are:<br /> - The victim must be willing<br /> - The willpower cost is huge<br /> - The benefits seems minor<br /> <br /> Point 1:<br /> Psychognosis only work on willing victims, wich per se is fine, but them, to have some easy access you need to use it on something that you already have like your Herd. Making it also needs a second merit for good use.<br /> <br /> Point 2:<br /> You need to spend 1WP to activate the hypnosis and 1 more for each technique, so, at least 2 WP to use the merit for a boost in a discipline. If you want to use all the benefits, this increases to 6 willpower points. You also needs to spend more willpower in certain levels to get some benefit, or vitae.<br /> <br /> Point 3:<br /> The benefits this merit gives to the disciplines are not as rewarding, some more questions on Auspex, or minus 1 to 3 dices to resist Dominate.<br /> <br /> Kindred normally don't dream. Having access to the dreams of the kine should give some way to get Willpower or other form of resource, that's the whole propaganda of the bloodline, they have discovered a way to tap into the infinite source of energy that is the dreams and use it for their own benefit. What do you guys think about the bloodline?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the book of Astral planes states that Vampires do dreams, nightmares ruled by the Beast or tragic lies reimagined by the Man","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T11:27:55-08:00","id":1433527,"title":"","content":"So, slight clarification, because I realize now that I wrote it ambiguously: You only have to pay a maximum of <b>5</b> Willpower to access all levels of Psychognosis at once (barring an exceptional success). The first Willpower is spent into a technique, and then any subsequent expenditures are into &quot;<i>additional </i>techniques&quot;. I see now that it's bit muddy (and in fact, the wording as-is was revised from my even more obtuse original phrasing), but word count is a harsh mistress, and sometimes you make cuts to explanatory prose that make sense to you, but not to readers.<br /> <br /> The other thing about the Willpower cost (that also maybe isn't obvious) is that you can mete it out when you need it. You have until your patient wakes up, so you're not obligated to spend them all at once. You choose the one you definitely need, and then you can go on a case by case basis.<br /> <br /> All that said, the one I'd probably be willing to houserule is Waking Prescience. The reason it costs Willpower to ask further questions is because, normally, Spirit's Touch is a one and done affair. You can't just keep poking an object until you know everything, and if you fail, you're out of luck (at least in a single scene). The Merit assures you always get at least one question, and if it's the <i>wrong </i>question, you can have a chance for a do-over. On the other hand, Willpower <i>is </i>a little scarce in <b>Vampire</b>. So, here's my suggestion: either use the system for additional questions from Diagnostic Dreaming, or allow players to roll <i>and </i>auto succeed at the same time on the Spirit's Touch. The latter is a pretty reasonable interpretation of the ability anyway, so treat that as &quot;official&quot; if you prefer it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 01-26-2021, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T02:08:07-08:00","id":1528784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1433492-the-icelus-foundation-and-psychognosis?p=1433527#post1433527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, slight clarification, because I realize now that I wrote it ambiguously: You only have to pay a maximum of <b>5</b> Willpower to access all levels of Psychognosis at once (barring an exceptional success). The first Willpower is spent into a technique, and then any subsequent expenditures are into &quot;<i>additional </i>techniques&quot;. I see now that it's bit muddy (and in fact, the wording as-is was revised from my even more obtuse original phrasing), but word count is a harsh mistress, and sometimes you make cuts to explanatory prose that make sense to you, but not to readers.<br /> <br /> The other thing about the Willpower cost (that also maybe isn't obvious) is that you can mete it out when you need it. You have until your patient wakes up, so you're not obligated to spend them all at once. You choose the one you definitely need, and then you can go on a case by case basis.<br /> <br /> All that said, the one I'd probably be willing to houserule is Waking Prescience. The reason it costs Willpower to ask further questions is because, normally, Spirit's Touch is a one and done affair. You can't just keep poking an object until you know everything, and if you fail, you're out of luck (at least in a single scene). The Merit assures you always get at least one question, and if it's the <i>wrong </i>question, you can have a chance for a do-over. On the other hand, Willpower <i>is </i>a little scarce in <b>Vampire</b>. So, here's my suggestion: either use the system for additional questions from Diagnostic Dreaming, or allow players to roll <i>and </i>auto succeed at the same time on the Spirit's Touch. The latter is a pretty reasonable interpretation of the ability anyway, so treat that as &quot;official&quot; if you prefer it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for necroing this thread but I just stumbled upon the Icelus and from what I gather you're the writer behind them (hi!). Your last post really clarifies a lot of mechanics-related questions, but I have some lore-related ones (I really like to imagine the nitty gritty details for roleplaying purposes). Since you're the writer behind the bloodline I hope you can help me with that!<br /> <br /> To my understanding, the Icelus are both a business and a mystery cult. I understand that psychognosis is effectively a form of dream hypnotherapy and is fundamentally a mundane/psychological technique utilizing drugs and hypnosis. What I don't understand is how dreams are &quot;consumed&quot; and how the process enhances the Dominate and Auspex of Icelus vampires.<br /> <br /> I've reread their section in <i>Night Horrors: Spilled Blood</i> and from what I gather the psychognosis technique is both mundane and supernatural. There is a level of actual dream psychoanalysis and hypnosis that goes into psychognosis, perhaps it is punctuated with therapy sessions during the day as well. Maybe the patient goes for their day appointment, spends an hour in therapy, then an hour in sleep, and then an hour of analysis. However when a victim/patient is &quot;prepped&quot; enough they are advised to switch to the more serious and intense &quot;night therapy sessions&quot; which include therapy (again) and then spending the entire night at an Icelus center in a state of dreamless &quot;sleep&quot;.<br /> <br /> So when the patient is sufficiently hypnotized and drugged they are put in a comfortable bed, with various devices monitoring their vitals, but the Icelus therapist who initiated the process uses Mesmerize in addition to the regular techniques, and when the patient falls into a deep trance the vampire spends some time observing them and maybe uses something like Beast's Hackles or Uncanny Perception to establish an actual, real psychic connection between the patient's dreams and the vampire's psyche. Or they simply take a sip of the sleeper's blood and establish the connection thus. Whatever the case, it is the use of discipline powers or blood that adds a genuine element of the supernatural and allows the vampire to siphon dreams.<br /> <br /> So after a good hour spent with the patient, observing them and establishing the connection, the Icelus therapist leaves into the night and essentially has a temporary psychic link with the victim. The victim's dreams are siphoned and perhaps due to the connection the Icelus can even tap into the &quot;universal subconscious&quot; of humanity. This manifests as a kind of &quot;dull headache&quot;, &quot;fleeting visions&quot; or &quot;white noise&quot; at the back of the vampire's mind. It's always there and occasionally the vampire may be momentarily distracted for a mere fraction of a second as they experience the dreams. However this is not enough to endanger the vampire.<br /> <br /> In the end whenever the therapist wishes to &quot;consume&quot; some of the dreams they have siphoned, the dream fully invades their mind and grants them supernatural insight and effectively enhances their chosen powers. So essentially it's like eating dreams &quot;on demand&quot;.<br /> <br /> At the end of the night, whenever the patient wakes, the psychic bond is broken.<br /> <br /> Does this interpretation make sense? Or is the technique purely mundane and there is no &quot;dream eating&quot;? The text implies both so I've tried to incorporate both the mundane and the supernatural/the psychic, but I am honestly a little confused haha. Any insight from you will be greatly appreciated, I know this was written ages ago but, I don't know, maybe you have some kind of a tip or insight to share haha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3567,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3567-dobyk","user":"Dobyk","date":". 01-18-2024, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3567-dobyk","name":"Dobyk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3567_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T11:29:15-08:00","id":1528817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dobyk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1433492-the-icelus-foundation-and-psychognosis?p=1528784#post1528784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry for necroing this thread but I just stumbled upon the Icelus and from what I gather you're the writer behind them (hi!). Your last post really clarifies a lot of mechanics-related questions, but I have some lore-related ones (I really like to imagine the nitty gritty details for roleplaying purposes). Since you're the writer behind the bloodline I hope you can help me with that!<br /> <br /> To my understanding, the Icelus are both a business and a mystery cult. I understand that psychognosis is effectively a form of dream hypnotherapy and is fundamentally a mundane/psychological technique utilizing drugs and hypnosis. What I don't understand is how dreams are &quot;consumed&quot; and how the process enhances the Dominate and Auspex of Icelus vampires.<br /> <br /> I've reread their section in <i>Night Horrors: Spilled Blood</i> and from what I gather the psychognosis technique is both mundane and supernatural. There is a level of actual dream psychoanalysis and hypnosis that goes into psychognosis, perhaps it is punctuated with therapy sessions during the day as well. Maybe the patient goes for their day appointment, spends an hour in therapy, then an hour in sleep, and then an hour of analysis. However when a victim/patient is &quot;prepped&quot; enough they are advised to switch to the more serious and intense &quot;night therapy sessions&quot; which include therapy (again) and then spending the entire night at an Icelus center in a state of dreamless &quot;sleep&quot;.<br /> <br /> So when the patient is sufficiently hypnotized and drugged they are put in a comfortable bed, with various devices monitoring their vitals, but the Icelus therapist who initiated the process uses Mesmerize in addition to the regular techniques, and when the patient falls into a deep trance the vampire spends some time observing them and maybe uses something like Beast's Hackles or Uncanny Perception to establish an actual, real psychic connection between the patient's dreams and the vampire's psyche. Or they simply take a sip of the sleeper's blood and establish the connection thus. Whatever the case, it is the use of discipline powers or blood that adds a genuine element of the supernatural and allows the vampire to siphon dreams.<br /> <br /> So after a good hour spent with the patient, observing them and establishing the connection, the Icelus therapist leaves into the night and essentially has a temporary psychic link with the victim. The victim's dreams are siphoned and perhaps due to the connection the Icelus can even tap into the &quot;universal subconscious&quot; of humanity. This manifests as a kind of &quot;dull headache&quot;, &quot;fleeting visions&quot; or &quot;white noise&quot; at the back of the vampire's mind. It's always there and occasionally the vampire may be momentarily distracted for a mere fraction of a second as they experience the dreams. However this is not enough to endanger the vampire.<br /> <br /> In the end whenever the therapist wishes to &quot;consume&quot; some of the dreams they have siphoned, the dream fully invades their mind and grants them supernatural insight and effectively enhances their chosen powers. So essentially it's like eating dreams &quot;on demand&quot;.<br /> <br /> At the end of the night, whenever the patient wakes, the psychic bond is broken.<br /> <br /> Does this interpretation make sense? Or is the technique purely mundane and there is no &quot;dream eating&quot;? The text implies both so I've tried to incorporate both the mundane and the supernatural/the psychic, but I am honestly a little confused haha. Any insight from you will be greatly appreciated, I know this was written ages ago but, I don't know, maybe you have some kind of a tip or insight to share haha.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the dream eating is definitely literal, but how they actually get the victim sleep is wholly arbitrary. I don't remember how much I went into this, but all the therapy is just nonsense. It's mostly about having enough time to psychically tune themselves to the victim and then getting her to sleep. They could do CBT or Freudian analysis and the supernatural aspects would still work; the Scientology-esque auditing they call Psychgnosis is more of a way to focus themselves rather than anything that truly benefits the subject. I would've loved to have written up something detailed like all that, but word count is a harsh mistress with bloodlines. I've never thought too hard about what the precise mechanisms are, but that's a really good interpretation! Basically, if in doubt, it's supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T00:44:22-08:00","id":1529141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1433492-the-icelus-foundation-and-psychognosis?p=1528817#post1528817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All the dream eating is definitely literal, but how they actually get the victim sleep is wholly arbitrary. I don't remember how much I went into this, but all the therapy is just nonsense. It's mostly about having enough time to psychically tune themselves to the victim and then getting her to sleep. They could do CBT or Freudian analysis and the supernatural aspects would still work; the Scientology-esque auditing they call Psychgnosis is more of a way to focus themselves rather than anything that truly benefits the subject. I would've loved to have written up something detailed like all that, but word count is a harsh mistress with bloodlines. I've never thought too hard about what the precise mechanisms are, but that's a really good interpretation! Basically, if in doubt, it's supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the response! This is definitely very helpful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3567-dobyk","name":"Dobyk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3567_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}